missionable tour","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["eat","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Sarchí oxcart crafts","si_tag":"culture_heritage","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.thecostaricatoursite.com/san-jose/tours/Poas-Volcano-Doka-Coffee-Plantation-and-La-Paz.php (Accessed 2026-07-06)","timing":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the town that hand-paints the carreta, Costa Rica''s national-symbol oxcart; the world''s largest oxcart and the artisan workshops. Usually stacked with Poás/Doka/Grecia","si":"culture","blurb":"the town that hand-paints the carreta, Costa Rica''s national-symbol oxcart; the world''s largest oxcart and the artisan workshops. Usually stacked with Poás/Doka/Grecia","when":"mid-December–April  + Christmas/NY + Semana Santa","commission":"commissionable combo day-tour + retail","accessed":"2026-07-06","wells":["activities","shop"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is San José worth staying a night, or just an airport?","a":"Worth a night. It''s the front door, not the destination — but the Pre-Columbian Gold Museum (~1,600 pieces, beside the Teatro Nacional), a three-museum pass (~$33), and the Barrio Escalante restaurant row give a genuine half-to-full day of culture-and-coffee substance.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can you day-trip Poás and Irazú volcanoes from San José?","a":"Yes — both are same-day from the capital. Irazú tops 3,432 m with both oceans visible on a clear morning; Poás runs a dynamic-access, online-only timed-entry model via SINAC, so go guided to absorb the timed-entry and closure logistics.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where is SJO airport and how busy does it get?","a":"Juan Santamaría (SJO) is Costa Rica''s primary international gateway, 20 km northwest of downtown in Alajuela. It just set a record, handling 3,215,208 international passengers between Nov 2025 and Apr 5 2026 — up 7.9% year-over-year — so book gateway beds and transfers ahead of the dry-season wave.","source":"ticotimes.net, 2026-07-06","si_tag":null},{"q":"If something goes wrong in Costa Rica, is medical care nearby?","a":"Reassuringly, yes — San José IS the national medical and evacuation hub. Hospital Clínica Bíblica (founded 1929, JCI-accredited, 24/7, with an on-site heliport for evac) and the US-affiliated Hospital CIMA are both in the metro, so serious care and the evac hub are right here.","source":"internationalinsurance.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San José & Costa Rica''s Central Valley: Volcanoes, Coffee Tours & the Gateway to Pura Vida | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Poás & Irazú volcanoes, Doka & Café Britt coffee estates, the Gold & Jade museums, and Pacuare whitewater — all day-trippable from SJO. The accurate guide to Costa Rica''s Central Valley gateway. TravelWell.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"es-CR","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San José Costa Rica","Volcán Poás tour","tour de café Costa Rica","Volcán Irazú desde San José","Museo del Oro Precolombino","rafting río Pacuare un día","hoteles cerca del aeropuerto Juan Santamaría","Barrio Escalante dónde comer"],"hreflang":["en","es-CR"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-06","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/costa-rica","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:18Z","source_updated":"2026-05-19T11:42:25+01:00"}]},"long_tail":["things to do in San José Costa Rica one day","Poás Volcano tour from San José 2026","Irazú Volcano Cartago day trip","best coffee tour near San José Doka vs Café Britt","Pacuare River rafting day trip from San José","where to stay near SJO airport Costa Rica"]},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["culture_heritage","expedition"],"ultra":[{"name":"Finca Rosa Blanca","type":"coffee-estate boutique","location":"Santa Bárbara de Heredia","tier":"ultra (valley)","mor":"brand-direct/DMC net rate","consortia":"sold via Jacada/Lightfoot luxury operators; Virtuoso not independently confirmed — verify","fora_lane":true},{"name":"Xandari Resort & Spa","type":"hillside villa-suite eco-boutique","location":"Alajuela","tier":"premier–ultra (valley)","mor":"brand-direct/DMC net rate","consortia":"not confirmed — verify","fora_lane":true},{"name":"Hotel Grano de Oro","type":"tropical-Victorian casona boutique","location":"San José city","tier":"premier (city)","mor":"brand-direct/DMC","consortia":"not confirmed — verify","fora_lane":true},{"name":"Costa Rica Marriott Hotel Hacienda Belén","type":"hacienda-style branded luxury resort","location":"La Asunción (near SJO)","tier":"premium–premier (airport)","mor":"brand-direct (Marriott)","consortia":"Marriott STARS/Luminous where eligible","fora_lane":true}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"San José & the Central Valley, Costa Rica"},"geo":{"lat":9.9281,"lng":-84.0907},"orbit":[{"id":"guanacaste-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["tropical","expedition","liveaboard","wellness","wildlife"]},{"id":"la-fortuna-arenal-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["expedition","romance","wellness"]},{"id":"manuel-antonio-costa-rica","jewels":9,"si":["tropical","expedition","wildlife"]},{"id":"monteverde-costa-rica","jewels":12,"si":["expedition","wildlife","romance"]},{"id":"nosara-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["tropical","expedition","wellness"]},{"id":"osa-peninsula-corcovado-costa-rica","jewels":9,"si":["expedition","diveglobal"]},{"id":"puerto-viejo-costa-rica","jewels":10,"si":["tropical","expedition","culture","wildlife","ocean"]},{"id":"tortuguero-costa-rica","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","river"]}],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 98),
  ('san-jose-del-cabo-mexico', '10S', 'San José del Cabo', 'Mexico', 'A lantern-lit gallery street', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"romance","expedition","culture","ocean"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Gallery District Art Walk runs Thursdays 5–9 pm, November–June, free (Source: ivanguaderrama.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Estero de San José is the only freshwater coastal lagoon in BCS, a State Ecological Reserve/IBA with 270+ bird species (Source: mexicobirdingtrail.org, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Playa Palmilla is Blue Flag and one of the few consistently swimmable Corridor beaches (Source: casanatalia.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Whale season mid-Dec–mid-Apr, humpback + gray, ~90–95% peak sightings (Source: visitloscabos.travel, Accessed 2026-07-04)","Hurricane peak Aug–Oct, September historically most active for Los Cabos (Source: mexiconewsdaily.com, Accessed 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"H+ Los Cabos (Km 24.5 Transpeninsular, 24/7 ER); AmeriMed (San José + CSL, bilingual 24/7); Blue Medical/BlueNet (24/7 ER); air-evac to US for serious cases","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"MX","summary":"The FCDO advises against all but essential travel to named states, cities and border areas of Mexico — listed below in its own words, each with its own exceptions. The Yucatán Peninsula, Mexico City, Baja California Sur and the other main visitor regions carry no FCDO restriction.","source":"UK FCDO — Mexico travel advice, reviewed 2026-07-16 (verbatim snapshot from the research library)","_rule":"the FCDO restricted-area records for this country, verbatim. PRESENCE OF THIS BLOCK IS NOT A CLAIM THAT THIS DESTINATION SITS IN ANY OF THEM — membership is a coverage judgement and is set only in `zone_record`, by a human."}},"timing":{"peak":"November–April (dry season, whale-watching, Art Walk)","shoulder":"May–June & late October","green":"July–September into early October (hot, hurricane/chubasco)","booking_lead":"3–6+ months for peak ultra/villa; advance dining reservations Dec–Mar","off_season_specials":"Green-season warm-water ocean + spa value; disclose storm risk + insurance","event_peaks":"Christmas/New Year, Semana Santa, whale Jan–Mar, Art Walk Thu Nov–Jun","fire_date":"Late summer/early fall for Nov–Apr peak; late spring for green-season value"},"jewels":[{"name":"Gallery District Art Walk","si_tag":"Culture & Arts","status":"future","hook":"Thursday-night open-gallery cobblestone stroll, free, Nov–Jun","bookable_category":"free / bundle with dining","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.ivanguaderrama.com/san-jose-del-cabo-art-walk-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Thursday-night open-gallery cobblestone stroll, free, Nov–Jun","when":"year-round","commission":"adjacent dining/experience or hotel package","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["Culture & Arts","culture"],"shelf_fit":{"Culture & Arts":"evidenced","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","ocean":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["package","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"Culture & Arts","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''Culture & Arts'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"},{"name":"Estero de San José birding","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"270+ species freshwater lagoon reserve, endangered Belding''s Yellowthroat","bookable_category":"guided birding tour","tier":"comfort","source":"http://mexicobirdingtrail.org/plan-a-trip/san-jose-del-cabo-estuary/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"November–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"270+ species freshwater lagoon reserve, endangered Belding''s Yellowthroat","when":"November–April","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","ocean":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Whale-watching (Corridor)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Humpback + gray whale tours, ~90–95% peak sightings","bookable_category":"panga/catamaran tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.cabo-adventures.com/en/tour/whale-watching-in-cabo (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"expedition","blurb":"Humpback + gray whale tours, ~90–95% peak sightings","commission":"activity affiliate / Amstar DMC","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition","ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","ocean":"evidenced","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Playa Palmilla swim/snorkel","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"Blue Flag, protected swim beach fronting One&Only","bookable_category":"free beach + snorkel add-ons","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.casanatalia.com/nearby-attractions/san-jose-del-cabo-beaches/ (Accessed 2026-07-04)","si":"ocean","blurb":"Blue Flag, protected swim beach fronting One&Only","commission":"activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","ocean":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Corridor golf + spa day","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"27-hole/championship golf + resort spas for couples","bookable_category":"tee times + spa via resort/DMC","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.oneandonlyresorts.com/palmilla (Accessed 2026-07-04)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","blurb":"27-hole/championship golf + resort spas for couples","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC / resort","accessed":"2026-07-04","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","ocean":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Where''s the top end for a honeymoon in San José?","a":"San José/Palmilla is the branded-ultra spine of Los Cabos: One&Only Palmilla (the 1956-origin icon, 27-hole golf), Zadún (a Ritz-Carlton Reserve, 115 villas), Chileno Bay and Esperanza (Auberge). It''s the quiet, composed counterweight to Cabo San Lucas'' nightlife.","source":"virtuoso.com / guide.michelin.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When can I see whales, and is the estuary worth it?","a":"Whale season is mid-December to mid-April with ~90–95% sightings at peak (mother-calf pairs Jan–Feb). For nature on land, the Estero de San José — BCS''s only freshwater coastal lagoon and an Important Bird Area — holds 270+ bird species, best at dawn.","source":"visitloscabos.travel / mexicobirdingtrail.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Which San José beaches can I actually swim?","a":"Very few — most open Corridor beaches have strong currents and are not swim-safe. The reliable exception is Blue Flag Playa Palmilla, with a protected swimming area; Chileno and Santa María are the other Corridor swim beaches.","source":"casanatalia.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"What is the Art Walk, and when is it?","a":"Every Thursday evening, 5–9 pm, November through June, the Gallery District opens more than a dozen galleries along the cobblestone streets around Álvaro Obregón, with music and refreshments — and it''s free. Book Art Walk-night dinner ahead Dec–March.","source":"ivanguaderrama.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The ocean and the weather, not crime. Most open San José beaches have dangerous rip currents — swim only at Blue Flag Palmilla or other designated coves — and hurricane season runs Jun–Nov, September historically worst. Carry trip insurance for green-season dates.","source":"casanatalia.com / mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San José del Cabo Travel Guide — Art Walk, Whales & Blue Flag Beaches | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"The refined side of Los Cabos: Gallery District Art Walk, Estero San José birding, whale-watching, swim-safe Playa Palmilla, and branded-ultra resorts.","slug":"san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","primary_keyword":"San José del Cabo travel guide","long_tail":["San José del Cabo Art Walk Thursday","San José del Cabo vs Cabo San Lucas","Playa Palmilla swimming","whale watching San José del Cabo","luxury resorts San José del Cabo"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San José del Cabo","Art Walk San José del Cabo horarios","Estero de San José del Cabo aves","Playa Palmilla se puede nadar","avistamiento de ballenas Los Cabos","hoteles de lujo San José del Cabo"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-04","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-